@startuml Post-SCF Analysis

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor Black

!startsub POST_SCF_ANALYSIS
partition "Post-SCF Analysis" {
    switch (HF Method?)
    case (RHF)
        :Singlet state <latex>(S=0)</latex>
        No spin contamination check needed; <<#LightGreen>>
        
    case (UHF)
        :Calculate <latex>\langle\hat{S}^2\rangle</latex> expectation value
        <latex>\langle\hat{S}^2\rangle = S(S+1) + N_{\beta} - \sum_{ij}|\langle\psi^{\alpha}_i|\psi^{\beta}_j\rangle|^2</latex>; <<#LightCoral>>
        if (<latex>\langle\hat{S}^2\rangle \neq S_{ideal}(S_{ideal}+1)</latex>?) then (contaminated)
            :⚠ Spin contamination detected!
            Wavefunction contains higher spin states; <<#LightCoral>>
        else (pure)
            :Spin contamination acceptable; <<#LightCoral>>
        endif
        
    case (ROHF)
        :<latex>\langle\hat{S}^2\rangle = S(S+1)</latex> exactly
        Spin-pure by construction ✓; <<#LightYellow>>
    endswitch
}
!endsub

legend right
    **Index Notation:**
    |= Index |= Range |= Meaning |
    | i, j | 1 to n_occ | Molecular orbital indices |
    | N_β | - | Number of beta electrons |
    ----
    **Symbol Legend:**
    |= Symbol |= Description |
    | ⟨Ŝ²⟩ | Expectation value of spin-squared operator |
    | S | Total spin quantum number |
    | S(S+1) | Ideal spin expectation value for pure spin state |
    | S_ideal | Expected spin quantum number based on multiplicity |
    | ψ^α_i | Alpha (spin-up) molecular orbital i |
    | ψ^β_j | Beta (spin-down) molecular orbital j |
    | ⟨ψ^α_i|ψ^β_j⟩ | Overlap between alpha orbital i and beta orbital j |
    | Spin contamination | Mixing of unwanted higher spin states in UHF |
    | Singlet | Spin state with S=0 (all electrons paired) |
    | Doublet | Spin state with S=1/2 (one unpaired electron) |
    | Triplet | Spin state with S=1 (two unpaired electrons) |
    ----
    **HF Method Colors:**
    |<#LightGreen> RHF | Restricted Closed-Shell |
    |<#LightCoral> UHF | Unrestricted Open-Shell |
    |<#LightYellow> ROHF | Restricted Open-Shell |
endlegend

@enduml
